<newsitem itemid="75354" id="root" date="1996-09-25" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Mayfran year net falls 30.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Mayfran year net falls 30.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1.77  vs   2.56</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.45  vs   0.45</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    2.70  vs   3.90</p>
<p>    Turnover				20.79  vs  18.30</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.06  vs    nil</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.44  vs   0.47</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     0.53  vs   0.41</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.05  vs   0.02</p>
<p>    Tax					0.86  vs   0.84</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: Jan 21, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: Jan 6, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Bedlinen manufacturer and distributor Mayfran International Ltd said profits fell due to lower gross margins and higher operating costs.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
